Host assert checks (requires Python 3 and a C++11 compiler, no test framework):

    python3 test/run_host_tests.py

The runner builds every test/*/test_*.cpp with warnings as errors, AddressSanitizer
and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer in a temporary directory. CXX selects the compiler.
It also extracts actual main.cpp orchestration and GAP dispatch functions into
host harnesses with hardware doubles to check sync/show/audio/render integration,
radio ownership and EEPROM field migration. These checks
do not simulate BTstack, the FSM library, sensors, LED timing or physical power.

Firmware validation, all supported environments:

    pio run
    git diff --check

Show protocol and hardware checklist: docs/show-control-v1.md.
